    <title>Chief Complaint</title>
    <text><paragraph>Cut on the left forearm in a training drill an hour ago. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
</component>

<component>
  <section>
    <templateId root="1.3.6.1.4.1.19376.1.5.3.1.3.4"/>
    <code code="10164-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="History of Present illness Narrative"/>
    <title>History of Present Illness</title>
    <text><paragraph>Alexander came in an hour after a practice blade slipped past his guard in a drill and cut the outside of his left forearm. He pressed a cloth on it and the bleeding stopped within a few minutes. He can move his wrist and all his fingers and has no numbness. He had not been drinking; his last drinks were at a banquet three days ago, within his limit. His last tetanus booster was about seven years ago. His chest wall pain is better on the lidocaine patch and he asks what he can take for the arm without breaking his plan. [S]</paragraph><table><thead><tr><th>Element</th><th>Detail</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>Onset</td><td>An hour ago, a cut from a practice blade</td></tr><tr><td>Location</td><td>Outer left forearm</td></tr><tr><td>Duration</td><td>About one hour</td></tr><tr><td>Character</td><td>Stinging</td></tr><tr><td>Severity</td><td>4 of 10</td></tr><tr><td>Context</td><td>Training drill; no alcohol today; on acetaminophen as needed and a lidocaine patch</td></tr><tr><td>Modifying factors</td><td>Pressure stopped the bleeding</td></tr><tr><td>Associated signs and symptoms</td><td>No numbness or weakness; no other injury</td></tr></tbody></table></text>

  </section>
</component>

