    <code code="51847-2" codeSystem="2.16.840.1.113883.6.1" displayName="Evaluation + Plan note"/>
    <title>Assessment and Plan</title>
    <text><list listType="ordered"><item><content styleCode="Bold">Laceration of the left forearm (S51.812A)</content>. A simple laceration without tendon, nerve or vessel injury, seen within the hour. Tetanus booster due for a contaminated wound more than five years after the last dose. [S]<list><item>Irrigated and repaired under lidocaine 1% with six interrupted sutures.</item><item>Tdap today.</item><item>Keep it clean and dry for two days; sutures out at a nurse visit in ten days; return for redness, swelling, fever or discharge.</item><item>Acetaminophen within the 2,000 mg daily limit; no opioid and no regular anti-inflammatory tablets.</item></list></item><item><content styleCode="Bold">Alcohol use disorder, mild (F10.10)</content>. Within his drinking limits since the consultation; not drinking today. Safety reviewed: no thoughts of suicide or self-harm; the service pistol stays in the armory off duty; 988 card carried. [S]<list><item>Continue the plan with the addiction medicine clinician.</item></list></item></list><paragraph>Immunizations given today: Tdap (tetanus, diphtheria and acellular pertussis), one dose for a wound, last tetanus booster seven years ago [S]</paragraph><paragraph>Guideline basis: CDC Clinical Practice Guideline for Prescribing Opioids for Pain - United States, 2022 (2022); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for the Management of Substance Use Disorders (2021); VA/DoD Clinical Practice Guideline for Assessment and Management of Patients at Risk for Suicide (2024); Adult Immunization Schedule by Age (2026)</paragraph><paragraph>Follow-up: Nurse visit in ten days to remove the sutures. Six-week review in two weeks. The clinic or 988 at any hour. Next scheduled visit 2026-04-20: six-week review: chest wall pain and the exercise program, drinking and PEth, liver tests, grief and mood, safety, and the healed forearm wound. [S]</paragraph></text>

  </section>
